{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "What is a rational number?", "back_answer": "A number that can be expressed in the form p/q, where p and q are integers and q is not equal to 0.", "tags": ["rational-numbers", "definition"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "Are all natural numbers whole numbers?", "back_answer": "Yes, because the collection of whole numbers includes 0 along with all natural numbers.", "tags": ["number-systems", "natural-numbers", "whole-numbers"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "What kind of decimal expansion do rational numbers have?", "back_answer": "Either terminating or non-terminating recurring.", "tags": ["rational-numbers", "decimal-expansion"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "What is an irrational number?", "back_answer": "A number that cannot be expressed in the form p/q where p and q are integers and q is not equal to 0, having a non-terminating non-recurring decimal expansion.", "tags": ["irrational-numbers", "definition"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "Give two examples of irrational numbers.", "back_answer": "Square root of 2 (sqrt(2)) and pi.", "tags": ["irrational-numbers", "examples"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "What constitutes the set of real numbers?", "back_answer": "The collection of all rational and irrational numbers.", "tags": ["real-numbers", "number-line"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "How is sqrt(2) represented on a number line?", "back_answer": "By constructing a right-angled triangle with legs of 1 unit, using Pythagoras' theorem to get a hypotenuse of sqrt(2), and transferring it using an arc.", "tags": ["irrational-numbers", "number-line", "geometric-representation"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "What is the process of converting an irrational denominator into a rational number called?", "back_answer": "Rationalisation.", "tags": ["surds", "rationalisation"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "Rationalise the denominator of 1 / (sqrt(2) + sqrt(3)).", "back_answer": "sqrt(3) - sqrt(2)", "tags": ["rationalisation", "surds"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Number Systems", "front_prompt": "State the law of exponents: a^m * a^n = ?", "back_answer": "a^(m + n)", "tags": ["exponents", "laws-of-exponents"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "What is a polynomial in one variable of degree n?", "back_answer": "An expression of the form p(x) = a_nx^n + a_{n-1}x^{n-1} + ... + a_1x + a_0, where a_n != 0, a_i are real numbers, and n is a non-negative integer.", "tags": ["definition", "degree", "algebraic-expressions"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "What is the degree of a non-zero constant polynomial?", "back_answer": "Zero (0).", "tags": ["constant-polynomial", "degree"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "What is the degree of the zero polynomial?", "back_answer": "Not defined.", "tags": ["zero-polynomial", "degree"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "State the Remainder Theorem.", "back_answer": "Let p(x) be any polynomial of degree greater than or equal to one and let a be any real number. If p(x) is divided by the linear polynomial x - a, then the remainder is p(a).", "tags": ["remainder-theorem", "polynomial-division"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "State the Factor Theorem.", "back_answer": "If p(x) is a polynomial of degree n >= 1 and a is any real number, then (i) x - a is a factor of p(x) if p(a) = 0, and (ii) p(a) = 0 if x - a is a factor of p(x).", "tags": ["factor-theorem", "factors"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "What is a quadratic polynomial?", "back_answer": "A polynomial of degree 2, having the general form ax^2 + bx + c, where a != 0 and a, b, c are real numbers.", "tags": ["quadratic-polynomial", "degree"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "What are the zeros of a polynomial p(x)?", "back_answer": "A real number c is a zero of the polynomial p(x) if p(c) = 0.", "tags": ["zeros-of-polynomial", "roots"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "Expand (x + y + z)^2 using an algebraic identity.", "back_answer": "x^2 + y^2 + z^2 + 2xy + 2yz + 2zx", "tags": ["algebraic-identities", "expansion"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "Expand (x + y)^3.", "back_answer": "x^3 + y^3 + 3xy(x + y) or x^3 + y^3 + 3x^2y + 3xy^2", "tags": ["algebraic-identities", "cubes"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Polynomials", "front_prompt": "Factorize x^3 - y^3 using standard identities.", "back_answer": "(x - y)(x^2 + xy + y^2)", "tags": ["factorization", "algebraic-identities"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "What is the name of the horizontal and the vertical lines drawn to determine the position of any point in the Cartesian plane?", "back_answer": "The horizontal line is called the x-axis, and the vertical line is called the y-axis.", "tags": ["Cartesian plane", "axes", "basics"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "What is the intersection point of the x-axis and the y-axis called?", "back_answer": "Origin", "tags": ["origin", "axes", "basics"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "What are the four quadrants formed by the intersection of the x-axis and the y-axis?", "back_answer": "Quadrant I, Quadrant II, Quadrant III, and Quadrant IV (numbered counter-clockwise starting from the top-right).", "tags": ["quadrants", "Cartesian plane"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "What is the x-coordinate of a point also known as?", "back_answer": "Abscissa", "tags": ["abscissa", "x-coordinate", "terminology"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "What is the y-coordinate of a point also known as?", "back_answer": "Ordinate", "tags": ["ordinate", "y-coordinate", "terminology"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "What are the coordinates of the origin?", "back_answer": "(0, 0)", "tags": ["origin", "coordinates"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "What are the signs of the coordinates (x, y) of a point lying in the second quadrant (Quadrant II)?", "back_answer": "Negative x-coordinate and positive y-coordinate, i.e., (- , +)", "tags": ["quadrants", "signs", "Cartesian plane"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "In which quadrant do both coordinates x and y have negative signs (- , -)?", "back_answer": "Quadrant III", "tags": ["quadrants", "signs"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "What is the abscissa of any point lying on the y-axis?", "back_answer": "0 (zero)", "tags": ["y-axis", "abscissa"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Coordinate Geometry", "front_prompt": "If the coordinates of a point are (3, -4), in which quadrant does the point lie?", "back_answer": "Quadrant IV", "tags": ["quadrants", "coordinates"]}
