{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "Who wrote the famous treatise 'Elements', which is a collection of thirteen books on geometry?", "back_answer": "Euclid", "tags": ["history", "Euclid", "Elements"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "According to Euclid's definitions, what is the boundary of a solid?", "back_answer": "A surface", "tags": ["definitions", "solid", "surface"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "What are the boundaries of a surface?", "back_answer": "Curves or lines", "tags": ["definitions", "surface", "lines"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "State Euclid's First Axiom: 'Things which are equal to the same thing are...'", "back_answer": "...equal to one another.", "tags": ["axioms", "equality"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "According to Euclid's Axioms, if equals are added to equals, the wholes are...", "back_answer": "...equal.", "tags": ["axioms", "addition"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "State Euclid's Axiom regarding wholes and parts.", "back_answer": "The whole is greater than the part.", "tags": ["axioms", "whole and part"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "What does Euclid's First Postulate state about drawing a straight line?", "back_answer": "A straight line may be drawn from any one point to any other point.", "tags": ["postulates", "straight line"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "State Euclid's Fifth Postulate (Parallel Postulate).", "back_answer": "If a straight line falling on two straight lines makes the interior angles on the same side of it taken together less than two right angles, then the two straight lines, if produced indefinitely, meet on that side on which the sum of angles is less than two right angles.", "tags": ["postulates", "parallel lines", "fifth postulate"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "What is the difference between axioms and postulates in Euclid's geometry?", "back_answer": "Axioms are assumptions used throughout mathematics generally, whereas postulates are assumptions specific to geometry.", "tags": ["axioms", "postulates", "concepts"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Introduction to Euclid's Geometry", "front_prompt": "According to Euclid's Second Postulate, what can be done with a terminated line?", "back_answer": "A terminated line can be produced indefinitely.", "tags": ["postulates", "line segment"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "What is the sum of angles in a linear pair?", "back_answer": "180 degrees", "tags": ["angles", "linear-pair", "axioms"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "What can you say about vertically opposite angles when two lines intersect?", "back_answer": "Vertically opposite angles are equal.", "tags": ["intersecting-lines", "theorems"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "State the sum of all interior angles of a triangle.", "back_answer": "180 degrees (Angle sum property of a triangle).", "tags": ["triangles", "angle-sum-property"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "If a transversal intersects two parallel lines, what is the relationship between alternate interior angles?", "back_answer": "Alternate interior angles are equal.", "tags": ["parallel-lines", "transversal", "alternate-angles"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "What is the relationship between interior angles on the same side of the transversal when lines are parallel?", "back_answer": "They are supplementary (their sum is 180 degrees).", "tags": ["parallel-lines", "transversal", "co-interior-angles"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "State the exterior angle theorem of a triangle.", "back_answer": "If a side of a triangle is produced, the exterior angle so formed is equal to the sum of the two interior opposite angles.", "tags": ["triangles", "exterior-angle"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "What are lines that lie in the same plane and do not intersect anywhere called?", "back_answer": "Parallel lines", "tags": ["parallel-lines", "definitions"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "If two lines are both parallel to the same line, what is their relationship with each other?", "back_answer": "Lines which are parallel to the same line are parallel to each other.", "tags": ["parallel-lines", "theorems"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "What do you call an angle whose measure is greater than 0 degrees and less than 90 degrees?", "back_answer": "Acute angle", "tags": ["types-of-angles", "definitions"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Lines and Angles", "front_prompt": "If the sum of two adjacent angles is 180 degrees, what do they form?", "back_answer": "A linear pair", "tags": ["angles", "linear-pair"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "What does congruence of figures mean?", "back_answer": "Two figures are congruent if they are of the same shape and same size.", "tags": ["Congruence", "Basics"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "State the SAS congruence rule.", "back_answer": "Two triangles are congruent if two sides and the included angle of one triangle are equal to the two sides and the included angle of the other triangle.", "tags": ["SAS", "Congruence Criteria"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "State the ASA congruence rule.", "back_answer": "Two triangles are congruent if two angles and the included side of one triangle are equal to two angles and the included side of the other triangle.", "tags": ["ASA", "Congruence Criteria"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "State the AAS congruence rule.", "back_answer": "Two triangles are congruent if any two pairs of angles and one pair of corresponding non-included sides are equal.", "tags": ["AAS", "Congruence Criteria"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "State the SSS congruence rule.", "back_answer": "Three sides of one triangle are respectively equal to the three sides of another triangle.", "tags": ["SSS", "Congruence Criteria"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "State the RHS congruence rule.", "back_answer": "Two right triangles are congruent if the hypotenuse and one side of one triangle are respectively equal to the hypotenuse and one side of the other triangle.", "tags": ["RHS", "Right Triangles"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "What is the angle opposite to the longer side of a triangle?", "back_answer": "In a triangle, the angle opposite to the longer side is larger (greater).", "tags": ["Inequalities", "Sides and Angles"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "What is the side opposite to the larger angle of a triangle?", "back_answer": "In a triangle, the side opposite to the larger (greater) angle is longer.", "tags": ["Inequalities", "Sides and Angles"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "What is the relation between the sum of any two sides of a triangle and the third side?", "back_answer": "The sum of any two sides of a triangle is greater than the third side.", "tags": ["Triangle Inequality", "Property"]}
{"board": "KARNATAKA_STATE_BOARD_SSLC", "class": "Class_9", "subject": "Mathematics", "chapter": "Triangles", "front_prompt": "What can be said about angles opposite to equal sides of an isosceles triangle?", "back_answer": "Angles opposite to equal sides of an isosceles triangle are equal.", "tags": ["Isosceles Triangle", "Properties"]}
